NAME
       xfs_info - show the layout of an XFS file system

SYNOPSIS
       xfs_info MOUNT-POINT | DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       xfs_info prints the geometry of an XFS file system: the device, the
       inode size, the number of allocation groups (agcount), the block size
       (bsize) and number of data blocks, and the details of the log. The
       size in bytes is the number of data blocks times the block size.
       Nothing is changed.

EXAMPLES
           xfs_info /
           xfs_info /dev/vgdata/lvdata | grep data

SEE ALSO
       xfs_growfs(8), xfs_admin(8), mkfs.xfs(8)
